Native toolkit dependency builds
===============================

These recipes accompany the 2026-10-28 DomeD toolkit cleanup. Build as the
regular user. Stage and inspect artifacts; sudo is used only for installing
verified system packages. Nothing here restarts a desktop or display manager.

Fcitx core does not require Qt or GTK. Its optional client modules are separate
packages. SKK's Qt editor can be disabled with ENABLE_QT=OFF; no code fork is
needed for either engine.

Pinned sources:
  https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5 tag 5.1.23
    27cca6e0239938b2d53937061d0980c087856b22 (with pinned Yoga submodule)
  https://github.com/fcitx/fcitx5-skk tag 5.1.10
    176361f7711d7b1e9f98f08eb94f750474aeba3c

The build needs CMake/Ninja, a C++ compiler, gettext, ECM, nlohmann-json,
Wayland/protocols/scanner, XCB utility and imdkit development files, xkbcommon,
iso-codes/xkeyboard-config, systemd, libuuid, enchant2, libskk and libgee.
ECM supplies CMake macros and does not create a Qt runtime dependency.
For the installed build, missing development RPMs were downloaded and extracted
to a private dependency prefix rather than installing system development stacks.
--deps-root accepts that prepared prefix, whose .pc/CMake paths must resolve
inside the extracted tree. With normal system development packages it is not
needed. The two pinned source checkouts must already exist.

  python3 build-fcitx.py --source /path/to/fcitx5 \
    --skk-source /path/to/fcitx5-skk --work /path/to/work
  python3 package-fcitx.py --work /path/to/work

The core's 51 CTests must pass before packaging. The script installs only to
work/fcitx-stage and work/skk-stage, excludes development/test files from RPMs,
and provides the existing native FLTK configuration launcher. It assumes the
DomeD fcitx5-configuration-fltk executable is already installed. Check RPM
requirements and ELF runpaths before system installation. Package sources are
upstream Fcitx/SKK, not this recipe repository.

OpenCV and RapidOCR
------------------
OpenCV's GUI support is optional. The installed OCR environment uses
opencv-python-headless==5.0.0.93, whose cv2 build reports GUI: NONE. RapidOCR
3.9.2 hard-codes opencv_python in package metadata. The script below rewrites
only that dependency and its local version, preserving every upstream code
file byte-for-byte and regenerating RECORD hashes:

  python3 rebuild-rapidocr-headless.py \
    rapidocr-3.9.2-py3-none-any.whl rapidocr-3.9.2+domed1-py3-none-any.whl

In a copy of the OCR venv, remove opencv-python, install the local RapidOCR
wheel and the matching headless OpenCV wheel, run the package manager's check,
then test imports, contour operations, and /proc/self/maps. Keep the original
venv for rollback and switch only after verification. Do not retain the GUI
and headless OpenCV distributions together; they share the cv2 namespace.

Other replacements
------------------
https://github.com/jebot-git/kdeconnect-dome is the GSConnect-derived native
GIO service with FLTK dialogs and KDE-compatible D-Bus interfaces.
https://github.com/jebot-git/dome-dialog provides the tested Zenity command
subset used by Winetricks, without GTK. These are separate source repositories.

Validation on the target system
-------------------------------
51 Fcitx CTests, 13 protocol/plugin suites (124 tests), 16 independent TLS/SSHFS
checks, two real GJS/FLTK dialog response checks, and seven installed Zenity
compatibility checks passed. GTK3 native Wayland applications accepted English
and Japanese composition without Fcitx GTK modules. The original paired phone
reconnected and provided battery and certificate-pinned SFTP access. Full
feature parity with the original KDE Qt daemon is not claimed; Bluetooth is
not implemented and was already disabled in the old configuration.

The active Fcitx process was left intact because its inherited Wayland socket
cannot be recreated by an ordinary restart. Its maps already contained no Qt
or GTK; the rebuilt installed executable starts on the next login.

Calligra, KWallet and installed GTK applications were deliberately preserved.
Qt6 and GTK3 libraries needed by them remain installed. Desktop, wallet and
input-method sessions were not restarted. Private device keys, trust data,
network addresses, local backup trees and generated RPMs are not repository
contents.
